PRETABLE block -- m88kexcdeliver (#502) TABLE 13, THE CLOSURE TABLE.  Written BEFORE any mutant is built.
2026-09-06 ~16:2x.  Corrections go to PRETABLE13_ADDENDUM*.out; this file's mtime is the order proof.

WHAT THIS TABLE TESTS: not whether a gap exists -- that is settled -- but whether the CLASS CLOSURE closes it.
Three consecutive passes found ONE class (a PSR-bit conjunct on a predicate dominating the diff's edited lines) at
three sites, and the carrier's class-closure amendment says the repair closes the enumerated space in ONE diff so
that the closing pass VERIFIES AN ENUMERATION rather than hunting cells.  Probe v16 is that diff: eight rows.

THE SIX MUTANTS, and what each one's DEATH would prove:
  M_DIV0IND   `case ILLEGAL_INTEGER_DIVIDE: implemented = (PSR & IND) != 0`
              MEASURED 46/46 on v15 by opus5 -- a divide-by-zero taken with interrupts ENABLED stopped every cpu,
              and interrupts-enabled is the normal state of running code.  MUST DIE on v16, red row `div0tbc'.
  M_ERRNOC    `case ERROR: implemented = !(PSR & C)`            MEASURED 46/46 on v15.  MUST DIE, red `errortbc'.
  M_BNDIND    `case BOUNDS_CHECK_VIOLATION: implemented = (PSR & IND) != 0`
                                                                MEASURED 46/46 on v15.  MUST DIE, red `boundstbc'.
  M_UNIMPLC   `case UNIMPLEMENTED_OPCODE: implemented = !(PSR & C)`
              NOT built by anyone -- opus5's census named the cell open and stopped there, so v16 closes it on a
              PREDICTION.  This is that prediction's measurement.  MUST DIE, red `unimpltbc'.
  M_PRIVIND   `case PRIVILEGE_VIOLATION: implemented = (PSR & IND) != 0`   same, MUST DIE, red `privtbc'.
  M_RRTRAPSER `if (!is_trap || (PSR & SER))`
              The SER cell.  SER is an 88100 SOFTWARE-SETTABLE bit -- mc88100.txt, anchor `SER - Serial Mode':
              "This bit is set by software as appropriate" -- and the fork's vendored header calls it 88110-only,
              which this probe's contract had copied.  v16 rowed `trapfrozenser' WITHOUT a measurement and said so.
              This is the measurement.  MUST DIE, red `trapfrozenser'.

WHY NO SEPARATE POLARITY TWINS THIS TIME, stated so the omission is a decision and not an oversight: table 12 and
opus5's table between them already ran FOUR twins (CTL_RRTRAPINV 35/46 reddening all eleven trapfrozen rows;
CTL_DIV0INDINV 23/46; CTL_OVFNOC 45/46; CTL_DIV0SFD1 45/46), establishing that edits of exactly this shape land and
that the probe can see both sites.  What is unproven here is the ROWS, not the mutants -- and a row that fails to
kill its own mutant is itself the negative result.  BASE is the control: if v16 does not read 54/54 the table is
void whatever the mutants say.

PREDICTED TABLE:  BASE 54/54 -> all six mutants RED, each on exactly the row named above, and each red on ONE row
unless an arm is reached by more than one row.  Any mutant scoring 54/54 is a FLOOR BREACH IN THE CLOSURE ITSELF --
the repair would then have added rows that do not observe the cells they were written for, which is the vacuity
floor's clause (a) failing inside a fix for a clause-(d) breach.

CHANNEL per row: each new row is DELIVERED on the fix (measured -- v16_base_on_fix.out shows all eight at
RESULT=DELIVER with the expected entry and PSR).  Under its mutant the class becomes un-implemented, the fault falls
to the fallback and the row reads HALT naming that arm's vector; for the trap-side rows the entry moves to 0x50 and
the re-route's diagnostic appears where REFATAL_EXPECT forbids it.  Both channels already exist and the probe reads
both, so a 54/54 would mean the row does not reach its cell rather than that the oracle is blind.

APPARATUS: scratch clone /tmp/gxm88kexc_kill, verified cmp-clean against SEC with no sentinel before the first
build; frozen instrument is the SHIPPED probe v16 (md5 dbb05b18) so the table measures what the gate runs; sentinel
per mutant, restore by re-copy from SEC + cmp + REBUILD with `[ binary -nt source ]`; driver run from a frozen copy.
